# Purpose

This document establishes the shared engineering vocabulary used throughout the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to ensure engineers, designers, product managers, and AI assistants communicate using consistent terminology when discussing architecture, product capabilities, business domains, and implementation decisions.

A shared vocabulary reduces ambiguity, improves documentation quality, and strengthens communication across the engineering organization.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Canonical engineering terminology
* Business vocabulary
* Product vocabulary
* Architectural vocabulary
* Engineering terminology
* Language governance

It does not define implementation details, business requirements, or development practices.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It establishes a common language that allows every Engineering Standard to communicate architectural intent consistently across the platform.

---

# Required Reading

All Engineering Standards assume the terminology defined in this document.

When terminology conflicts arise, this glossary is the authoritative source.

---

# Engineering Responsibilities

This document owns:

* Shared engineering vocabulary
* Canonical terminology
* Preferred engineering language
* Terminology governance

It does not replace technical documentation or product documentation.

---

# Glossary Philosophy

Engineering quality depends on shared understanding.

Consistent terminology allows engineering decisions to remain understandable regardless of team, feature, or implementation technology.

Words should communicate precise meaning.

Equivalent concepts should always use the same terminology throughout the platform.

Different terms should never describe the same concept unless explicitly defined by this glossary.

